ef 17592186045417] [17592186572032 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "72d0d37d-2da5-57c2-b260-86d1c7a8fa86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572117 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572117 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572117 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572117 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$N=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572117 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d6c75b7-d9d1-5c4f-a63e-3df78db605e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572117 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the $1$st row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(N) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{5})=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(N)=-10.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572229 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572229 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53a19a3f-7183-5af9-b4ef-496541e95b0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572229 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572232 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "59d231e0-c609-5e56-9c9c-328f2b57b9ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572232 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/r